  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Fund Alert 938 Sudan (Displacement due to Conflict)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to deliver life-saving, multi-sectoral emergency assistance to conflict-affected internally displaced persons (IDPs) in Tawilla and Dar Es Salama, North Darfur. The response will focus on provision of lifesaving interventions including provision of Food items, Cash Assistance and hygiene kits to the most needy households displaced by the violent attacks on Zamzam camp._x000d_
The project will provide lifesaving interventions with implementation timelines of up to 45 days targeting a total of 18,450 beneficiaries. Specific attention will be paid to identifying and prioritizing:_x000d_
&#x2022;	Female-headed households_x000d_
&#x2022;	UASC headed households and child survivors_x000d_
&#x2022;	Households with children under 5_x000d_
&#x2022;	Elderly and persons with disabilities_x000d_
&#x2022;	Adolescent girls and women of reproductive age, particularly for dignity and hygiene kits_x000d_
This approach ensures that interventions are tailored to the specific vulnerabilities within households and that reporting reflects a gender-responsive and inclusive response.</narrative>
  </description>
